[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0mInteresting — the results actually match! The truncation at the end gives the same result because multiplication and XOR modulo 2^32 are the same whether you truncate at each step or at the end. This is because [38;5;10m(a * b) mod n == ((a mod n) * (b mod n)) mod n[0m. So the Rust approach of using u64 and truncating at the end is mathematically equivalent.[0m[0m
